From cfd285736a917661d346a00debd77154e31d545c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:57:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] GRPO: group advantages by prompt group, not by prompt tokens

GRPO found a sample's group by the tokens of its first prompt. A Gym agent
builds that prompt itself, and Harbor's Terminus-2 shows the pod's terminal in
it, with the pod's own hostname, so no two samples of a task shared a prompt:
every group had one sample and every advantage was 0 (job 1209940).

Each prompt group now gets an id before the rollout (sync path), or by its
replay entry (async path), and advantages, the trivial-group check and the
rows to train use those ids.

Port of NVIDIA-NeMo/RL #3882 (724344ffb, Ali Roshan Ghias and Lin Jia), the
grpo.py part with its tests. Its changes to the data-plane path (grpo_sync.py,
sync_rollout_actor.py) build on a schema change our pin does not have and are
left out; that path is off in our runs.
